  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Infrastructure</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">In August 2024, the AIFFP Safeguards team and the Transport Sector Program Phase 3 (TTSP3) Project Management Office is delivering training on the monitoring and implementation of environmental and social safeguards for the Wau Highway Long-term Maintenance Contract. The training is targeted to contractors and sub-contractors, the Department of Works and Highways (DoWH) and the Project Management and Supervision Consultant. It is complemented by a site visit, to apply updated monitoring checklists, community engagement processes and Grievance Redress Mechanisms on sections of the Wau Highway. The training highlights how safeguard and technical issues should be supervised on site to ensure compliance with AIFFP safeguard requirements, including PNG National Legislation, IFC Performance Standards and DFAT Environmental and Social Safeguard policies. The AIFFP is also collaborating with World Bank and Asian Development to develop the capacity of the DoWH safeguards and regional teams for LTMC and emergency works on PNG roads.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2023-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2024-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Economic policy reform and management and private sector development</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Australian Infrastructure Financing Facility for the Pacific (AIFFP) is providing AUD76.3 million ($61.6m loan and $14.7m grant) and the costs related to investment preparation works and program management to contribute to a safer, more reliable transport system supporting economic and social development for PNG. The project, aligned with PNG national development strategies, supports sustainable long-term rehabilitation and maintenance on the Wau Highway. The project is expected to create local jobs, employing people in the local area, and includes female participation targets to support awareness of women&#x2019;s right to equal employment opportunities. The investment will contribute to a well-functioning transport system which is critical for long-term economic growth and post-COVID economic recovery.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2023-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
